# PlatformIO build output
.pio/
.vscode/

# The 511.org API token. Never commit this — it is a per-developer credential
# and this repo may become public. The firmware reads its token from NVS
# (entered via the setup portal), never from a compiled-in constant; this file
# exists only so host-side tools can talk to the API during development.
.511-token

# Compiled host-test binaries (test/*.cpp is tracked, the binaries are not)
test/test_route
test/test_timetable

# Captured API responses may embed the token in a URL — keep raw captures local
# and commit only the sanitised fixtures under test/fixtures/.
tools/captures/

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Scratch artwork. This firmware draws no logo on any screen -- the code path
# was removed rather than left switched off -- so nothing here is built into
# anything. Ignored so that stray images cannot become an accidental commit.
assets/

# Transfer tarballs built by tools/package.sh
dist/
.venv-pio/
test/test_siri_parse
test/test_board_model
test/test_service_day
test/test_config
test/test_ota_manifest
test/test_ota_health
test/test_ota_verify
test/test_html_escape
test/test_csrf_check
test/test_wifi_pass_policy

# Fuzzer build output and grown corpus (crash-*, oom-*, timeout-* artifacts
# land here too). fuzz/seeds/ is hand-curated and stays tracked.
test/fuzz/fuzz_siri_parse
test/fuzz/corpus/

# AI dev-process exhaust. Planning directories, session notes and instruction
# files accumulate personal detail (whose machine, whose commute, whose shell
# habits) that has nothing to do with the firmware and everything to do with the
# author. Keep them out of the repo, and preferably outside the directory.
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
.superpowers/
docs/superpowers/

# Internal audit reports. Publishing a findings document is itself a disclosure;
# these live outside the repository entirely.
SECURITY-AUDIT-*
*-release-audit.*
